### Implementation Summary: Multi-User Conflict-Free Undo/Redo & Spatial Invalidation

The feature has been implemented and validated in `state-crdt.ts` and `canvas-engine.ts`.

#### 1. `CanvasStateManager` (`state-crdt.ts`)
- **`undo(peerId: string): WhiteboardElement[]`**:
  Pops the target peer's previous snapshot from isolated `peerUndoStacks`. Inspects each element: if an element has been concurrently updated by another peer (`cur.authorId !== peerId && cur.version > el.version`), the concurrent modification is preserved conflict-free. Otherwise, it restores the element with an incremented CRDT version to propagate forward cleanly. Returns `this.getAllElements()`.
- **`redo(peerId: string): WhiteboardElement[]`**:
  Pops from `peerRedoStacks` for the given peer, reapplies the state with bumped CRDT versions, pushes to the peer's undo stack, and returns `this.getAllElements()`.

```typescript
public undo(peerId: string): WhiteboardElement[] {
  const undoList = this.peerUndoStacks.get(peerId);
  if (!undoList || undoList.length === 0) return this.getAllElements();
  const targetSnapshot = undoList.pop()!;

  const currentAffected: WhiteboardElement[] = [];
  for (const el of targetSnapshot) {
    const cur = this.elements.get(el.id);
    if (cur) currentAffected.push({ ...cur });
  }
  if (!this.peerRedoStacks.has(peerId)) this.peerRedoStacks.set(peerId, []);
  this.peerRedoStacks.get(peerId)!.push(currentAffected);

  for (const el of targetSnapshot) {
    const cur = this.elements.get(el.id);
    if (!cur) {
      this.elements.set(el.id, { ...el, version: el.version + 1, authorId: peerId });
    } else if (cur.authorId === peerId || cur.version <= el.version) {
      this.elements.set(el.id, {
        ...el,
        version: Math.max(cur.version, el.version) + 1,
        authorId: peerId
      });
    }
  }
  return this.getAllElements();
}

public redo(peerId: string): WhiteboardElement[] {
  const redoList = this.peerRedoStacks.get(peerId);
